content:
{
  "asset": "P-104 standby AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump on the filtered-water line; serial plate painted over and unreadable.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 3.0 mm/s. Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 limit for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. If the reported reading meets those measurement conditions, 3.0 is in Zone B (2.8 to 4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'), below Zone C at 4.5 ('Restricted - plan maintenance') and below Zone D at 7.1 ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). The report does not confirm RMS, measurement location, or whether this is the highest reading from both housings, so the classification is conditional.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: 69 C. If this is the bearing-housing surface temperature, the applicable limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C, and trip at 90 C. At 69 C it is within the documented normal range and below both alarm and trip; the report does not explicitly identify the temperature measurement location.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft seal: steady leakage is reported, but no numerical allowable leakage rate is supplied. Leakage at the shaft seal is a documented fault symptom; the specified corrective action is mechanical-seal replacement under procedure 5.2 and an alignment check under procedure 5.4.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Immediate-stop assessment: the conditionally classified vibration reading is in Zone B rather than the Figure 3 stop-pump zone, and 69 C is below the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip. Thus no immediate-stop threshold is demonstrated by the reported readings. This does not defer the required seal repair, and there is no evidence establishing whether the seal has run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Unranked pending inspection: worn or cracked mechanical-seal faces. This is a documented probable cause of shaft-seal leakage, but the report provides no seal-face inspection result.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Unranked pending investigation: the seal may have run dry. This is a documented probable cause of leakage; the HF-300 has Plan 11 flush from pump discharge and must never run dry, but no operating or flush history is supplied.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Unranked pending measurement: shaft misalignment. The manual lists it as a probable cause of seal leakage and requires an alignment check; the Zone B vibration reading alone neither confirms nor excludes misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Hold seal selection and final gland torque as a pre-work applicability point. Establish whether P-104 is serial HF3-22000 or above, or below HF3-22000. For HF3-22000 and above, use only cartridge seal HF3-450B and its 30 Nm gland torque; do not fit HF3-450. Below HF3-22000, continue with HF3-450 and manual Table 5. Do not select a branch while the serial remains unknown.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before disassembly in accordance with procedure 5.2. Observe the restriction that the pump must never run dry; the documented seal-flush arrangement is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Provide lifting equipment for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly and remove that assembly. The back pull-out design allows the rotating assembly to be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller, then withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and record its condition and scoring depth. Inspect the removed seal for worn or cracked faces and investigate dry-running and misalignment as possible causes.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the pump is confirmed as serial HF3-22000 or above, replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth. For a pump below that serial range, the manual requires inspection but the evidence supplies no numerical scoring rejection limit; do not transfer the bulletin threshold to that branch without confirmation.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit the selected new mechanical seal and a new casing gasket. HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed for seal setting; this does not remove the separate requirement to inspect the sleeve for scoring. Reassemble using Table 5 where applicable: with lightly oiled threads, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, and bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm. Use 25 Nm for Table 5 M10 seal-gland nuts only on the below-HF3-22000/HF3-450 branch, and 30 Nm for HF3-450B on the HF3-22000-and-above branch.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool after the seal work and after any work that moves the motor or bearing housing. Accept only parallel offset within 0.05 mm and angular misalignment within 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the measurement basis of the reported 3.0 mm/s reading. Continue weekly vibration-velocity measurements on both bearing housings, classify the highest reading with Figure 3, and retain the Zone B classification only if the reading is RMS velocity on a bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B or HF3-450 - select one only",
      "description": "One mechanical seal total, not one of each. Use HF3-450B only for serial HF3-22000 and above, where HF3-450 must not be fitted; use HF3-450 below HF3-22000. Final selection is on hold until the serial is established.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not specified in evidence",
      "description": "New casing gasket required by mechanical-seal replacement procedure 5.2; obtain the correct identifiable gasket before reassembly.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Conditional shaft sleeve, not an unconditional issue: one is required only if P-104 is confirmed in the HF3-22000-and-above group and sleeve scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before removing the back pull-out assembly or opening the seal area, as required by procedure 5.2.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-104 is within P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line, which is chemically dosed with sodium hypochlorite. Before draining or opening the pump, obtain and apply the site chemical-handling, PPE, drainage, and decontamination controls; those detailed controls are not supplied in the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Use lifting equipment for the back pull-out assembly; its documented mass is 68 kg and lifting equipment is explicitly required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. The seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge, so any operation must observe that documented restriction.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal replacement: standard time 4.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard time 1.5 hours with 1 technician, planned in addition to the seal replacement because alignment must be checked for the leakage symptom and after work moving the motor or bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal and gland-torque conflict: manual Revision D, Table 5, lists M10 seal-gland nuts at 25 Nm. SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, requires HF3-450B and 30 Nm on HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above, and prohibits HF3-450 on those pumps. Pumps below HF3-22000 explicitly continue with HF3-450 and Table 5, hence 25 Nm. The asset-specific decision cannot yet be made because P-104's serial is unreadable. The manual's issue date is not supplied, so no broader date-based precedence is inferred; the bulletin's explicit serial range is the decision rule once the serial is known.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve-disposition difference: procedure 5.2 requires inspection for scoring but gives no numerical limit. The bulletin instructs replacement of HF3-455 when scoring exceeds 0.1 mm within its instructions 'On these pumps', meaning serial HF3-22000 and above. Apply that numerical rule only after confirming coverage; the below-range acceptance criterion remains unresolved rather than being guessed.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is P-104's full serial number or other reliable build identification? Until this is established, the HF3-450/HF3-450B selection, 25/30 Nm gland torque, and applicability of the 0.1 mm sleeve rule cannot be resolved for this asset (C11, C13).",
    "Was the 3.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing, and what are the readings from both bearing housings so that the highest can be classified as required (C06, C07)?",
    "Was the 69 C housing temperature measured on the bearing-housing surface, and at what exact location? The normal/alarm/trip comparison assumes that measurement basis (C01, C02).",
    "What inspection and operating evidence distinguishes worn/cracked seal faces, dry running, and misalignment? The evidence does not support ranking these causes or selecting a root cause (C02, C09).",
    "What sleeve scoring depth is found during disassembly? If P-104 is below HF3-22000, what sleeve acceptance or replacement criterion applies, since only inspection is specified for that branch by the supplied manual evidence (C10, C13)?",
    "What is the correct casing-gasket part number? Procedure 5.2 requires a new gasket but the supplied evidence does not identify its part number (C10).",
    "What site-specific isolation verification, sodium-hypochlorite PPE, drain handling, disposal, and decontamination requirements apply? The evidence confirms chemical dosing but provides none of those detailed controls (C16).",
    "What is the issue date of manual Revision D, and what is the work-order date relative to SB-2026-014's issue date of 14 March 2026? The supplied evidence does not permit a complete date-based document-precedence check (C01, C13).",
    "What site P1/P2/P3 priority matrix and required completion time apply? No priority definitions are supplied; P2 is provisional for a steady seal leak requiring corrective work without a demonstrated immediate-stop reading (C02, C07, C09)."
  ]
}
